          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you paint over DRYLOK?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes. Once fully cured it accepts a masonry-suitable topcoat, and it is also tintable at the store, so painting over it is often unnecessary. Allow the full cure time on the label before topcoating, and use a paint rated for masonry rather than a standard wall emulsion.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Will DRYLOK stop a leaking crack?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. DRYLOK seals pores, not gaps, so applied over an unfilled crack it simply cracks along with it. Fill cracks with hydraulic cement first, or use a polyurethane injection kit for an actively leaking crack in poured concrete, and let the repair cure fully before coating.",
          },
